    "background_story": "Keanu was a geologist with an unquenchable thirst for adventure. Growing up in a small coastal town, he spent most of his childhood exploring the rugged shoreline, fascinated by the secrets hidden within the rocks. His obsession led him to study geology, and soon he became an expert in rare minerals. Keanu's claim to fame came when he discovered a significant deposit of monazite, a rare phosphate mineral, in a remote region of the Australian outback. The find sparked a flurry of interest in the scientific community, and Keanu's name became synonymous with the discovery. As he delved deeper into the world of monazite, he began to unravel the mysteries of the mineral's unique properties, making groundbreaking contributions to the field of geology. Keanu's love for monazite had taken him on a journey that would change the course of his life forever.",
